    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d348">

                <pb facs="0705" n="679" sameAs="frus:frus1961-63v04/pg679"/>

                <head>348. Memorandum From the Chairman of the Joint Chiefs of Staff (Taylor) to President Johnson<anchor n="1" xml:id="d348-f1"
                    /></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">CM-1065-63</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1963-12-06"><hi rendition="#italic">December 6,
                        1963</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <list subtype="subject" type="description">
                    <label>SUBJECT</label>
                    <item>Assignment of Personnel to South Vietnam</item>
                </list>
                <p>The Joint Chiefs of Staff are completely in accord with the view expressed in
                    your memorandum of December 2, 1963<anchor n="2" xml:id="d348-f2"/> that South
                    Vietnam is our most critical military area at the moment. In recognition of this
                    priority, they have undertaken to see to it that General Harkins receives the best officers available
                    in each of the areas of military activity represented in his command.</p>
                <p>Since receiving your memorandum of 2 December 1963, the Joint Chiefs of Staff
                    have conveyed its content to Admiral Felt and General Harkins, asking them to report to the Joint Chiefs of Staff whether
                    the policy expressed therein is being presently carried out to their
                        satisfaction.<anchor n="3" xml:id="d348-f3"/> If such is not the case, now
                    or in the future, they are to report the facts at once to the Joint Chiefs of
                    Staff.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#bold">Maxwell D.
                                Taylor</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
